<Defs>

	<ThingDef ParentName="DrugImplantThingMakeableBase">
		<defName>DI_LuciferiumImplant</defName>
		<label>drug-implant (Luciferium)</label>
		<description>An unique synthesizer, encoded to manage active mechanites inserted from Lucifierium, whilst also renewing some of them. The implant requires nutrients to function, and as a result, the user will need to eat more to sustain themself.

Unlike most other implants, the only way to insert this implant is to jam it deep into the center of the brain; the process causing significant injuries to the brain, and rendering the user comatose while the brain heals and adapts to the new implant. In this state, the user requires Luciferium to stay alive, as without it, the synthesizer will malfunction and destroy the brain faster than even Luciferium itself.

Once fully adapted and healed, the synthesizer will heavily optimize the mechanites from Lucifierium. This causes multiple effects; from further improving basic functions, to delaying the loss of cohesion.

Unqinely, the user can consciously put the synthesizer into overdrive, exciting the mechanites to the point where they become extremely volatile. While active, the user becomes wickedly powerful in all regards, but will eventually perish from brain detonation if kept in this state for too long. There is a safe period where it will burn residue mechanites that have burnt out in the body, but it is hard to replenish.

On the urbworlds, they call Luciferium the 'Devil's Bargain'. The few that are brave enough to endure this implant often risk it all for a chance at godhood, killing anyone in their way for more of those seductive red pills. Great power… but at what cost?</description>
		<descriptionHyperlinks>
			<RecipeDef>InstallDI_LuciferiumImplant</RecipeDef>
		</descriptionHyperlinks>
		<techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
		<graphicData>
			<texPath>Things/Item/Health/HealthItem</texPath>
			<graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
			<drawSize>0.80</drawSize>
			<color>(189,169,118)</color>
		</graphicData>
		<statBases>
			<MarketValue>400</MarketValue>
		</statBases>
		<costList>
			<Luciferium>10</Luciferium>
			<DI_BaseImplantPart>1</DI_BaseImplantPart>
		</costList>
		<recipeMaker>
			<recipeUsers Inherit="False">
				<li>DrugLab</li>
			</recipeUsers>
		</recipeMaker>
		<thingCategories>
			<li>BodyParts</li>
		</thingCategories>
	</ThingDef>
  
	<HediffDef>
		<defName>LuciferiumSpecialCut</defName>
		<label>luciferium cut</label>
		<labelNoun>a luciferium cut</labelNoun>
		<description>A cut made during the insertion of an implant. This cut can only be properly healed by Lucifierium; all other methods may cause further damage.</description>
		<hediffClass>Hediff_Injury</hediffClass>
		<tendable>false</tendable>
		<displayWound>true</displayWound>
		<labelNounPretty>{0} in the {1}</labelNounPretty>
		<comps>
			<li Class="HediffCompProperties_GetsPermanent">
				<permanentLabel>luciferium cut scar</permanentLabel>
				<becomePermanentChanceFactor>999</becomePermanentChanceFactor>
			</li>
		</comps>
		<injuryProps>
			<averagePainPerSeverityPermanent>0.075</averagePainPerSeverityPermanent>
			<bleedRate>0</bleedRate>
			<canMerge>false</canMerge>
		</injuryProps>
	</HediffDef>
	
